(7406981, 1166706, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by markwiley:</b></div><hr/><i> Based upon the current score and nearly every single other entry in this challenge is a nature shot, I am guessing I did not interpret the challenge theme well. Somehow, I thought this image illustrated "... what''s happening as the season changes in YOUR corner of the world." I guess I was wrong.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I find your interpretation to be perfectly in-line with the challenge theme.</td>', 'Originally posted by markwiley: Based upon the current score and nearly every single other entry in this challenge is a nature shot, I am guessing I did not interpret the challenge theme well. Somehow, I thought this image illustrated "... what''s happening as the season changes in YOUR corner of the world." I guess I was wrong. I find your interpretation to be perfectly in-line with the challenge theme.', '2015-09-30 13:12:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7406997, 1166645, 112739, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the win! Really great work and I too knew this was taken from almost the same location as Richards. For more further interest, I made <a href="https://1x.com/photo/679857/all:user:131417" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> image from the top of Half Mountain. So, in both your image and Richard''s, you can see the top of Half Mountain. This image just gives you a little closer view of what Richard has already described as Keyboard-of-the-winds Longs Peak and Glacier Basin. Congrats!</td>', 'Congrats on the win! Really great work and I too knew this was taken from almost the same location as Richards. For more further interest, I made this image from the top of Half Mountain. So, in both your image and Richard''s, you can see the top of Half Mountain. This image just gives you a little closer view of what Richard has already described as Keyboard-of-the-winds Longs Peak and Glacier Basin. Congrats!', '2015-09-30 13:36:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7407005, 1166684, 112739, '<td valign="top">Great work as usual Richard and congratulations on the Red!</td>', 'Great work as usual Richard and congratulations on the Red!', '2015-09-30 13:48:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7407007, 1166704, 112739, '<td valign="top">One of my top rated images. Congrats on the yellow!</td>', 'One of my top rated images. Congrats on the yellow!', '2015-09-30 13:51:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7407024, 1166612, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the critique club*<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge.<br/> <br/>Your composition is very good, I like the way you have gone in close with good DOF on the apple and the hand together with the soft focus background of the abundant apple crop. It tells us that the apple is ripe and ready for picking which identifies it with the Northern hemisphere''s season. The empty patch of blue sky is a little dominating and would probably benefit from some cropping. The exposure is good and the colours and detail look good too.<br/> <br/>All in all, a very good submission Marcel, its a shame it didn''t get any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for it, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the critique club* An appealing image that meets the challenge. Your composition is very good, I like the way you have gone in close with good DOF on the apple and the hand together with the soft focus background of the abundant apple crop. It tells us that the apple is ripe and ready for picking which identifies it with the Northern hemisphere''s season. The empty patch of blue sky is a little dominating and would probably benefit from some cropping. The exposure is good and the colours and detail look good too. All in all, a very good submission Marcel, its a shame it didn''t get any comments during the challenge, I hope this makes up for it, Sid', '2015-09-30 17:28:39.000000', NULL, 0),
